-- Sigils (widening slice 15, core-march.md §3). `~toml"..."` is surface
-- sugar, not a new core construct: the parser produces `ESigil("toml",
-- content)` (lib/parser/parser.mly), and desugar.ml eliminates it BEFORE
-- typecheck ever runs, rewriting to the plain call `Sigil.toml(content')`
-- (desugar.ml:669-680). `ESigil` never reaches the typechecker (a hard
-- failwith guards this, typecheck.ml:4574) or the evaluator (eval.ml:7482)
-- -- every sigil types via the ordinary (T-App) rule against its desugared
-- callee's declared signature, `Sigil.toml : String -> TomlValue`. No new
-- typing rule is added; this witness proves the general-case desugaring is
-- real and type-checked. Reject companion: reject/t74 (an unimplemented
-- sigil name fails because the DESUGARED call is unbound, not because of
-- any sigil-specific check).
mod Main do
  fn main() do
    let cfg = ~toml"port = 8080"
    match Toml.get_int(cfg, "port") do
      Some(n) -> println(int_to_string(n))
      None -> println("none")
    end
  end
end
